1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,500
Action Movie Icons — Then & Now

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,831
Welcome to Action Icons, Then and Now.

3
00:00:14,931 --> 00:00:20,693
Arnold Schwarzenegger turned a champion
bodybuilder's physical presence into an
unmistakable movie persona.

4
00:00:20,793 --> 00:00:30,741
The Terminator, Predator, and Total Recall made
him a symbol of eighties action, while later work
added comedy and public service to the story.

5
00:00:30,841 --> 00:00:34,928
Sylvester Stallone created two of cinema's most
durable underdogs.

6
00:00:35,028 --> 00:00:43,302
Rocky and Rambo began as very different
characters, but both carried the determination
that made his screen image so lasting.

7
00:00:43,402 --> 00:00:47,489
Harrison Ford brought a dry, grounded humor to
extraordinary adventures.

8
00:00:47,589 --> 00:00:55,863
Han Solo and Indiana Jones remain legendary
because he made heroes look brave, skeptical, and
human at the same time.

9
00:00:55,963 --> 00:01:00,050
These early and later portraits span more than
changing hairstyles.

10
00:01:00,150 --> 00:01:03,500
They capture how action stardom learned to
endure.

11
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Three more icons. Look closely at the portraits and the roles that made them familiar.

12
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:07,012
The next icons prove that action can take many
forms.

13
00:04:07,112 --> 00:04:15,648
Samuel L Jackson can turn a few lines into a
defining movie moment, from Pulp Fiction to Nick
Fury and beyond.

14
00:04:15,748 --> 00:04:20,171
His voice, timing, and presence make even an
ensemble feel larger.

15
00:04:20,271 --> 00:04:28,396
Hugh Jackman brought musical theater energy and
fierce physical commitment to Wolverine, then
showed another side in The Greatest Showman.

16
00:04:28,496 --> 00:04:36,620
Sigourney Weaver changed science fiction with
Ripley in Alien, a character defined by
intelligence and survival rather than easy
stereotypes.

17
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:40,321
Ghostbusters and Avatar later displayed her
comedy and imagination.

18
00:04:40,421 --> 00:04:44,845
Six action careers, each built on a different
kind of strength.

19
00:04:44,945 --> 00:04:49,468
Which hero or heroine would you add to the next
chapter?

20
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:59,700
Which early and later pairing surprised you most?
